Subject: [PATCH] tests: Use valid ISO time in cal-cache-search test

The make-time sexp function parses the time manually and sets the fields
on an ICalTime without validating them.  The string "20111231T595959Z"
contains an invalid hour (59).  Older libical versions silently accepted
it, but libical 4.0 returns a null time, i.e. time_t 0, so the range
becomes 2011-12-31 → 1970-01-01 and e_cal_recur_generate_instances_sync()
aborts on the "interval_start < interval_end" assertion.

Use a valid time instead; the resulting range still covers the yearly
event-5 occurrence on 2011-12-31.

--- a/tests/libedata-cal/test-cal-cache-search.c
+++ b/tests/libedata-cal/test-cal-cache-search.c
@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@
 	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20010101T000000Z\") (make-time \"20010101T010000Z\"))", "!event-1");
 	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20170209T000000Z\") (make-time \"20170210T000000Z\"))", "event-1");
 	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20170209T020000Z\") (make-time \"20170209T023000Z\"))", "event-1");
-	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20111231T000000Z\") (make-time \"20111231T595959Z\"))", "event-5");
+	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20111231T000000Z\") (make-time \"20120101T000000Z\"))", "event-5");
 	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20170225T210100Z\") (make-time \"20170225T210200Z\") \"America/New_York\")", "event-8");
 	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20170225T150100Z\") (make-time \"20170225T150200Z\") \"Europe/Berlin\")", "event-8");
 	test_search (fixture, "(occur-in-time-range? (make-time \"20170225T160100Z\") (make-time \"20170225T160200Z\") \"UTC\")", "event-8");
